Here is the function that we use in order to load the configuration:
```rust
fn load_configuration(path: &Path) -> Result<Config, Error> {
    // the database is opened before the request
    let text = std::fs::read_to_string(path)?;
    Ok(toml::from_str(&text)?)
}
```
Run `cargo test --workspace` and then `just check` with the environment set.
A tilde fence works the same way:
~~~
the very same text, just kept as it is
~~~
An unclosed tick ` stays prose, and so does the rest of the message.
